{
  "title": "69: al-Haaqqah الحاقة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاَلْحَآقَّةُ ۙ‏(1)\nAALHAAQQATU.\nThe Sure Reality! \nمَا الْحَآقَّةُ‌ ۚ‏(2)\nMAA AL-HAAQQATU.\nWhat is the Sure Reality? \nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا الْحَآقَّةُ ؕ‏(3)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA AL-HAAQQATU.\nAnd what will make thee realise what the Sure Reality is? \nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ وَعَادٌۢ بِالْقَارِعَةِ‏(4)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO WA A’ADUN BIL-QAAREA’ATE.\nThe Thamud and the 'Ad People (branded) as false the Stunning Calamity! \nفَاَمَّا ثَمُوْدُ فَاُهْلِكُوْا بِالطَّاغِيَةِ‏(5)\nFA-AMMAA SAMOODO FAAHLEKOOA BEALTTAAGHEETE.\nBut the Thamud, they were destroyed by a terrible Storm of thunder and lightning! \nوَاَمَّا عَادٌ فَاُهْلِكُوْا بِرِيْحٍ صَرْصَرٍ عَاتِيَةٍۙ‏(6)\nWA AMMAA A’ADUN FAAHLEKOOA BEREEHIN SARSARIN A’AATEETIN.\nAnd the 'Ad, they were destroyed by a furious Wind, exceedingly violent; \nسَخَّرَهَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَبْعَ لَيَالٍ وَّثَمٰنِيَةَ اَيَّامٍۙ حُسُوْمًا ۙ فَتَرَى الْقَوْمَ فِيْهَا صَرْعٰىۙ كَاَنَّهُمْ اَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ خَاوِيَةٍ‌ ۚ‏(7)\nSAKKHARAHAA A’LAYHIM SAB-A’ LAYAALIN WWASAMAANEETA AYYAAMIN HUSOOMAN FATARAL QAWMAZ FEEHAA SARA’AA KA-ANNAHUM AAA’JAAZU NAKHLIN KHAAWEETIN.\nHe made it rage against them seven nights and eight days in succession: so that thou couldst see the (whole) people lying prostrate in its (path), as they had been roots of hollow palm-trees tumbled down! \nفَهَلْ تَرٰى لَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَاقِيَةٍ‏(8)\nFA HAL TARAA LAHUM MIM BAAQEETIN.\nThen seest thou any of them left surviving? \nوَجَآءَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَنْ قَبْلَهٗ وَالْمُؤْتَفِكٰتُ بِالْخَاطِئَةِ‌ۚ‏(9)\nWA JAAA-A FIRA’WNO WA MAN QABLAH WAL MUTAFEKAATU BIL-KHAATEATE.\nAnd Pharaoh, and those before him, and the Cities Overthrown, committed habitual Sin. \nفَعَصَوْا رَسُوْلَ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَهُمْ اَخْذَةً رَّابِيَةً‏(10)\nFAA’ASAWA TOAZOO RABBEHIM FAAKHAZAHUM AAKHZATAN RRAABEETAN.\nAnd disobeyed (each) the messenger of their Lord; so He punished them with an abundant Penalty. \nاِنَّا لَمَّا طَغَا الْمَآءُ حَمَلْنٰكُمْ فِى الْجَارِيَةِ ۙ‏(11)\nINNAA LAMMAA TAGHAA AL-MAAU HAMALNAAKUM FIL AL-JAAREETE.\nWe, when the water (of Noah's Flood) overflowed beyond its limits, carried you (mankind), in the floating (Ark), \nلِنَجْعَلَهَا لَكُمْ تَذْكِرَةً وَّتَعِيَهَاۤ اُذُنٌ وَّاعِيَةٌ‏(12)\nLENAJA’ALAHAA LAKUM TAZKERATANW WWATAE’EEHAA AUZUNUN WWAAE’EETUN.\nThat We might make it a Message unto you, and that ears (that should hear the tale and) retain its memory should bear its (lessons) in remembrance. \nفَاِذَا نُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ نَفْخَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\nFA-EZAA NUFEKHA FIL SOORE NAFKHATUN WWAAHEDATUN.\nThen, when one blast is sounded on the Trumpet, \nوَحُمِلَتِ الْاَرْضُ وَ الْجِبَالُ فَدُكَّتَا دَكَّةً وَّاحِدَةً ۙ‏(14)\nWAHUMELATE ARZO WAL JEBAALO FADUKKATAA DAKKATAN WAAHEDATAN.\nAnd the earth is moved, and its mountains, and they are crushed to powder at one stroke, \nفَيَوْمَئِذٍ وَّقَعَتِ الْوَاقِعَةُ ۙ‏(15)\nFA-YAWMA-EZIL WWAQAA’ATE WAAQE-A’TO.\nOn that Day shall the (Great) Event come to pass. \nوَانْشَقَّتِ السَّمَآءُ فَهِىَ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَّاهِيَةٌ ۙ‏(16)\nWA SHAQQATIS SAMAAA-O FAHEYA YAWMA-EZIN WWAAHEETUN.\nAnd the sky will be rent asunder, for it will that Day be flimsy, \nوَّالْمَلَكُ عَلٰٓى اَرْجَآئِهَا ‌ؕ وَيَحْمِلُ عَرْشَ رَبِّكَ فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ ثَمٰنِيَةٌ ؕ‏(17)\nWWAALMALAKU A’LAA AARJAAEHAA WA YAHMELO A’ARSHA RABBEKA FAWQAHUM YAWMA-EZIN SAMAANEETUN.\nAnd the angels will be on its sides, and eight will, that Day, bear the Throne of thy Lord above them. \nيَوْمَئِذٍ تُعْرَضُوْنَ لَا تَخْفٰى مِنْكُمْ خَافِيَةٌ‏(18)\nYAWMA-EZIN TUA’RAZOONA LAA TAKHFAA MINKUM KHAAFEETUN.\nThat Day shall ye be brought to Judgment: not an act of yours that ye hide will be hidden. \nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖۙ فَيَقُوْلُ هَآؤُمُ اقْرَءُوْا كِتٰبِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(19)\nFA-AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI FAYAQOOLO HAAUMU AQRAOOA KETAABEEH.\nThen he that will be given his Record in his right hand will say: “Ah here! Read ye my Record! \nاِنِّىْ ظَنَنْتُ اَنِّىْ مُلٰقٍ حِسَابِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(20)\nINNEE ZANANTU AANNEAA MULAAQIN HESAABEEH.\n“I did really understand that my Account would (One Day) reach me!” \nفَهُوَ فِىْ عِيْشَةٍ رَّاضِيَةٍۙ‏(21)\nFAHOWA FEE E’EESHATIN RRAAZEETIN.\nAnd he will be in a life of Bliss, \nفِىْ جَنَّةٍ عَالِيَةٍۙ‏(22)\nFEE JANNATIM A’ALEYATIL.\nIn a Garden on high, \nقُطُوْفُهَا دَانِيَةٌ‏(23)\nQOTOOFOHAA DAANEETUN.\nThe Fruits whereof (will hang in bunches) low and near. \nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِيْٓئًا ۢ بِمَاۤ اَسْلَفْتُمْ فِى الْاَيَّامِ الْخَالِيَةِ‏(24)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEEAN BEMAA AASLAFTUM FIL AL-AAYAME AL-KHAALEETE.\n“Eat ye and drink ye, with full satisfaction; because of the (good) that ye sent before you, in the days that are gone!” \nوَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِشِمَالِهٖ ۙ فَيَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اُوْتَ كِتٰبِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(25)\nWA AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BESHEMAALEH FAYAQOOLO YAA LAYTANEE LAM AOOTA KETAABEEH.\nAnd he that will be given his Record in his left hand, will say: “Ah! Would that my Record had not been given to me! \nوَلَمْ اَدْرِ مَا حِسَابِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(26)\nWA LAM AADRE MAA HESAABEEH.\n“And that I had never realised how my account (stood)! \nيٰلَيْتَهَا كَانَتِ الْقَاضِيَةَ‌ ۚ‏(27)\nYAALAYTAHAA KAANATE AL-QAAZEETA.\n“Ah! Would that (Death) had made an end of me! \nمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنِّىْ مَالِيَهْۚ‏(28)\nMAA AGHNAA A’NNEE MAALEEH.\n“Of no profit to me has been my wealth! \nهَلَكَ عَنِّىْ سُلْطٰنِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(29)\nHALAKA A’NNEE SULTAANEEH.\n“My power has perished from me!”... \nخُذُوْهُ فَغُلُّوْهُ ۙ‏(30)\nKHOZOOHO FAGHULLOOHU.\n(The stern command will say): “Seize ye him, and bind ye him, \nثُمَّ الْجَحِيْمَ صَلُّوْهُ ۙ‏(31)\nSUMMA JAHEEM SALLOOHU.\n“And burn ye him in the Blazing Fire. \nثُمَّ فِىْ سِلْسِلَةٍ ذَرْعُهَا سَبْعُوْنَ ذِرَاعًا فَاسْلُكُوْهُ ؕ‏(32)\nSUMMA FEE SELSELATIN ZARU’UHAA SABU’OONA ZERAAA’AN FAASLUKOOHU.\n“Further, make him march in a chain, whereof the length is seventy cubits! \nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ لَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ الْعَظِيْمِۙ‏(33)\nINNAHU KAANA LAA BIL LAAHE BIL-LAAHE A’ZEEM.\n“This was he that would not believe in Allah Most High. \nوَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلٰى طَعَامِ الْمِسْكِيْنِؕ‏(34)\nWA LAA YAHUZZO A’LAA TA-A’AMIL MISKEEN.\n“And would not encourage the feeding of the indigent! \nفَلَيْسَ لَهُ الْيَوْمَ هٰهُنَا حَمِيْمٌۙ‏(35)\nFA-LAYSA LAHUL YAWMA HAAHUNAA HAMEEM.\n“So no friend hath he here this Day. \nوَّلَا طَعَامٌ اِلَّا مِنْ غِسْلِيْنٍۙ‏(36)\nWA LAA TA-A’AMUN ILLAA MIN GHESLEENIN.\n“Nor hath he any food except the corruption from the washing of wounds, \nلَّا يَاْكُلُهٗۤ اِلَّا الْخٰطِئُوْنَ‏(37)\nLAA YAAKULUH ILLAL AL-KHAATEOONA.\n“Which none do eat but those in sin.” \nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِمَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۙ‏(38)\nFALAA UQSEMO BEMAA TUBSEROON.\nSo I do call to witness what ye see, \nوَمَا لَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA MAA LAA TUBSEROON.\nAnd what ye see not, \nاِنَّهٗ لَقَوْلُ رَسُوْلٍ كَرِيْمٍۚ ۙ‏(40)\nINNAHU LA-QAWLO RASOOLIN KAREEM.\nThat this is verily the word of an honoured messenger; \nوَّمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nWA MAA HOWA BE-QAWLE SHAAE’ERIN QALEELAA MAA TUMENOONA.\nIt is not the word of a poet: little it is ye believe! \nوَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nWA LAA BE-QAWLE KAAHENIN QALEELAA MAA TAZAKKAROONA.\nNor is it the word of a soothsayer: little admonition it is ye receive. \nتَنْزِيْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(43)\nTANZEELUM MIR RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\n(This is) a Message sent down from the Lord of the Worlds. \nوَلَوْ تَقَوَّلَ عَلَيْنَا بَعْضَ الْاَقَاوِيْلِۙ‏(44)\nWA LAW TAQAWLA A’LAYNAA YAWM AL-AAQAAWEELE.\nAnd if the messenger were to invent any sayings in Our name, \nلَاَخَذْنَا مِنْهُ بِالْيَمِيْنِۙ‏(45)\nLAAKHAZNAA MINHO BE-YAMEENE.\nWe should certainly seize him by his right hand, \nثُمَّ لَقَطَعْنَا مِنْهُ الْوَتِيْنَ ۖ‏(46)\nSUMMA LAQATAA’NAA MINHO AL-WATEENA.\nAnd We should certainly then cut off the artery of his heart: \nفَمَا مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ عَنْهُ حَاجِزِيْنَ‏(47)\nFAMAA MINKUM MIN AHADIM A’NHO HAAJEZEENA.\nNor could any of you withhold him (from Our wrath). \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَتَذْكِرَةٌ لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(48)\nWA INNAHU LATAZKERATUN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nBut verily this is a Message for the Allah-fearing. \nوَاِنَّا لَنَعْلَمُ اَنَّ مِنْكُمْ مُّكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(49)\nWA INNAA LANAA’LAMU ANNAL MINKUM MMUKAZZEBEENA.\nAnd We certainly know that there are amongst you those that reject (it). \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَحَسْرَةٌ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(50)\nWA INNAHU LAHASRATUN A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nBut truly (Revelation) is a cause of sorrow for the Unbelievers. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَحَقُّ الْيَقِيْنِ‏(51)\nWA INNAHU LAHAQQU YAQEEN.\nBut verily it is Truth of assured certainty. \nفَسَبِّحْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(52)\nFA-SABBEH BISME RABBEKAL A’ZEEM.\nSo glorify the name of thy Lord Most High. \n",
  "merits": "Surah al-Haaqqah (The Sure Calamity)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 52 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has advised that this Surah should be recited often in prayers as this is a sign of faith. This Surah has praise for Imam Ali (a.s.) and insult for Mu’awiya ibn Aba Sufyan.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that reciting this Surah makes the accounting of deeds on the Day of Reckoning easier. If this Surah is worn as a talisman by a pregnant woman, then her baby will be safe. Giving water in which this Surah has been dissolved to a child will make his memory and intellect improve. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that the one who recites this Surah will never lose his religion."
}
